<!--Render Target Documentation — SerializationRules
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.SerializationRules-->
<rdoc:SerializationRules xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    How MBOM values become SCAD settings expressions
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Type shapes live on com.machineblocks.bml.type.* and native parameters on
    NativeBlock.bml. This block is only the emit strategy (transferred from the
    former types handbook, section 6).

    Strategy:

    1. Read the BOM member value in authored form.
    2. Consult type metadata (field order, serialize capability, NativeBlock
       scad:value).
    3. Translate at render time.
    4. Choose the shortest valid SCAD expression.
    5. Add scadName to expression text on the SettingsBundle.
    6. The SettingsEmitter writes the bundle (V1 pseudo-map pair, future object).

    Default struct to SCAD array: element order is the type's property
    declaration order — the same ordinal as BML positional array literals.
    Do not invent a separate SCAD index convention.

        FaceMapXY properties xNeg, xPos, yNeg, yPos
        MBOM { xNeg: 1, xPos: 1, yNeg: 0, yPos: 0 }
        SCAD [1, 1, 0, 0]

    Exceptions must be defined on the type, the property, or an annotation
    facet. Never implied:

    - Compact forms (PerSide4 scalar or 2-element when faces are paired)
    - Enum / catalog literals via scad:value
    - A custom serialize capability on the type or property

    Examples (settings entry shown as the V1 pair):

    SizeXYZ { x:4, y:2, z:3 } -> ["size", [4, 2, 3]]

    AxisXYZ holeXYZDiameter
    - all auto -> ["holeXYZDiameter", "auto"]
    - { x:3, y:3, z:4 } -> ["holeXYZDiameter", [3, 4]]
    - { x:3, y:3.2, z:4 } -> ["holeXYZDiameter", [3, 3.2, 4]]

    PerSide4 recessWallThickness
    - all 0.333 -> ["recessWallThickness", 0.333]
    - x faces 0.5, y faces 0.25 -> ["recessWallThickness", [0.5, 0.25]]
    - 0.5, 0.4, 0.25, 0.2 -> ["recessWallThickness", [0.5, 0.4, 0.25, 0.2]]

    FaceVector6 sizeMod
    - { "x-":0, "x+":0.5, others 0 } -> ["sizeMod", [0, 0.5, 0, 0, 0, 0]]

    FaceMap baseAdjustment
    - { "x-": -0.1, "x+": -0.1, "z+": 0.05 }
      -> ["baseAdjustment", [["x-", -0.1], ["x+", -0.1], ["z+", 0.05]]]
    - namespaced keys pass through: "pbx.x+", "pty.z+"

    SelectiveGrid studs
    - studs true stays ["studs", true]
    - studAreas become [["studAreas", [[[0,0],[1,1], false], [[2,0],[3,1], "hollow"]]]]

    WallGapList recessWallGaps
    - [{ face:"x+", position:0, length:"full" }, { face:"y-", position:2, length:3 }]
      -> ["recessWallGaps", [["x+"], ["y-", 2, 3]]]

    Direction.West -> ["direction", "west"]

    Color { hex: "#EAC645" } -> ["baseColor", "#EAC645"]

    Expressions stay ExpressionValue { raw } on the BOM. The renderer serializes
    the parsed AST or a statically resolved value. See ExpressionRenderer.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:DomainBoundary" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:SerializationRules>
